      },
      "message": "fix(data): hpmcounter*h CSRs should be definedBy Zihpm, not Sscofpmf\n\nThe user-mode HPM counter high-half CSRs (hpmcounter3h through hpmcounter31h)\nwere incorrectly listed as being defined by the Sscofpmf extension. According\nto Table 20 in the RISC-V spec (Counter Delegation chapter), these CSRs\ndepend on Zihpm support, just like their 64-bit counterparts (hpmcounter3\nthrough hpmcounter31).\n\nThe distinction is:\n- Zihpm: provides the user-mode HPM counter CSRs (both full and high-half)\n- Sscofpmf: provides counter overflow and privilege mode filtering\n\nThis fix updates the hpmcounterNh.layout template and regenerates all 29\naffected YAML files.\n\nFixes #1287",
